ef":"","count":1,"firstVerse":42},{"id":"amalek-h6002g","name":"Amalek","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":43}],"words":[{"base":"H4829","lemma":"מִרְעֶה","tr":"mir·eh","gloss":"pasture","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":13},{"base":"H8033","lemma":"שָׁם","tr":"sham","gloss":"there","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":834},{"base":"H3427","lemma":"יָשַׁב","tr":"ya·shav","gloss":"to dwell","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1079},{"base":"H6629","lemma":"צֹאן","tr":"tson","gloss":"flock","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":274},{"base":"H0438","lemma":"אַלּוֹן","tr":"al·lon","gloss":"oak","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H2124","lemma":"זִיזָא","tr":"zi·za","gloss":"Ziza","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3042","lemma":"יְדָיָה","tr":"ye·da·yah","gloss":"Jedaiah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H5294","lemma":"נְעַרְיָה","tr":"ne·ar·yah","gloss":"Neariah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H5717","lemma":"עֲדִיאֵל","tr":"a·di·el","gloss":"Adiel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H4672","lemma":"מָצָא","tr":"ma·tsa","gloss":"to find","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":455}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1SA","chapter":30,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And David struck them down from twilight until the evening of the next day. Not a man escaped, except four hundred young men who fled, riding off on camels.","from":43},{"book":"GEN","chapter":6,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The Nephilim were on the earth in those days—and afterward as well—when the sons of God had relations with the daughters of men. And they bore them children who became the mighty men of old, men of renown.","from":38},{"book":"GEN","chapter":9,"verse":22,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Ham, the father of Canaan, saw his fatherʼs nakedness and told his two brothers outside. Then Shem and Japheth took a garment and placed it across their shoulders, and walking backward, they covered their fatherʼs nakedness. Their faces were turned away so that they did not see their fatherʼs nakedness. When Noah awoke from his drunkenness and learned what his youngest son had done to him, he said, “Cursed be Canaan! A servant of servants shall he be to his brothers.” He also declared: “Blessed be the Lord, the God of Shem! May Canaan be the servant of Shem.","from":40},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The sons of Ham: Cush, Mizraim, Put, and Canaan.","from":40},{"book":"GEN","chapter":36,"verse":8,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Esau (that is, Edom) settled in the area of Mount Seir. This is the account of Esau, the father of the Edomites, in the area of Mount Seir.","from":42},{"book":"EXO","chapter":17,"verse":14,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the LORD said to Moses, “Write this on a scroll as a reminder and recite it to Joshua, because I will utterly blot out the memory of Amalek from under heaven.” And Moses built an altar and named it The LORD Is My Banner. “Indeed,” he said, “a hand was lifted up toward the throne of the LORD. The LORD will war against Amalek from generation to generation.”","from":43},{"book":"NUM","chapter":32,"verse":1,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Now the Reubenites and Gadites, who had very large herds and flocks, surveyed the lands of Jazer and Gilead, and they saw that the region was suitable for livestock. So the Gadites and Reubenites came to Moses, Eleazar the priest, and the leaders of the congregation, and said, “Ataroth, Dibon, Jazer, Nimrah, Heshbon, Elealeh, Sebam, Nebo, and Beon, which the LORD conquered before the congregation of Israel, are suitable for livestock—and your servants have livestock.”","from":41},{"book":"DEU","chapter":1,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"It is an eleven-day journey from Horeb to Kadesh-barnea by way of Mount Seir.","from":42}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}